From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:18:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] test(compose): run the whole inference loop in the
 compose smoke

The smoke only created and read a service, which then stopped at
SchedulerUnavailable. It now runs the closed loop through the gateway,
without GPUs:

- docker-compose.fake-runtime.yaml, layered on docker-compose.yaml,
  gives the control plane a one-device inventory
  (fake-runtime-inventory.json, mounted read-only) and the fake
  launcher, whose instances listen on all addresses of the container
  and are advertised as `control-plane`, an address the gateway may
  dial by default. docker-compose.yaml itself stays as it was: no
  inventory, no launcher, no instances.
- compose_smoke.sh uses both files and checks: requests without a key
  are rejected (resource API and chat route); create -> Ready with
  Ready=True and one ready openai-chat endpoint on control-plane;
  streaming chat via /api/v1/namespaces/default/inference/smoke-svc/chat
  returns an event stream whose events spell the instance's reply and
  end with [DONE]; the workflow store sits next to the registry; DELETE
  -> 202 -> 404 and the instance port is closed; re-creating the name
  on the single device gets Ready with a new instance and chat reaches
  it; after a control plane restart the resource is still there but
  Degraded (Ready=False, InstanceLost, endpoint not ready) and the
  gateway answers 503 NO_HEALTHY_UPSTREAM; the degraded service can be
  deleted.

Chat checks retry for a while because the gateway caches a service's
endpoints for 5 s. The script now needs jq (preinstalled on GitHub
runners).
